#lang rmn/v2
(map
  ("type" "HierarchicalCircuitKernelLowLevelDesign")
  ("version" 3)
  ("precondition" "HLD units M1-U1 through M1-U8 and their interfaces are the approved design target for the bounded semantic kernel implementation.")
  ("operation" "Implement strict exact-key normalization, deterministic ordering, placement-neutral component definitions, typed endpoint elaboration, exhaustive bounded FOUR transfer tables, monotonicity checks, finite lattice iteration, canonical relational RMN encoding, exact behavior equivalence, recursive contextual-address enumeration, and total sovereign-assembly verification.")
  ("postcondition" "The kernel accepts only definition families whose canonical identities are order-independent, whose ports are completely routed, whose tensor/par boundary is explicit, whose declared behavior is exactly its synthesized composition, and whose separate assembly places one membrane at every contextual occurrence.")
  ("refusal" "Refuse unknown fields rather than preserving them; refuse any scale label; refuse a membrane or account in a definition or instance; refuse tensor consensus metadata; refuse par without chain and contract; refuse repeated or missing pins; refuse child identity drift; refuse incomplete or nonmonotone behavior; refuse equivalence failure; refuse an assembly with a wrong root or any missing, duplicate, or invented occurrence address.")
  ("position" (map ("sas" "M1") ("hld-units" ("M1-U1" "M1-U2" "M1-U3" "M1-U4" "M1-U5" "M1-U6" "M1-U7" "M1-U8")) ("implementation" "rmn-semantic-conformance/src/hierarchical-circuit.mjs")))
  ("data-invariants"
    ("All maps expose exact fields; normalization never retains an unknown field."
     "Ports, instances, nets, and behavior rows have unique canonical keys and deterministic UTF-8 ordering."
     "A leaf has neither instances nor nets; a composite has both."
     "Each external and child pin participates exactly once in the direction appropriate to that pin."
     "Every net preserves predicate identity, carrier identity, and tensor/par mode across all endpoints."
     "Every behavior table contains all 4^n input valuations for at most six inputs and is monotone under bitwise knowledge inclusion."
     "Every child reference resolves to bytes whose computed ni identity equals the reference."
     "Every contextual occurrence address generated by recursive containment has exactly one membrane in the separate assembly; definitions and instances contain none."
     "A public provider interface is exactly one normalized leaf definition inside one signed Agent Card extension; it contains no instances or nets and is owned by the provider rather than synthesized by a consumer."))
  ("algorithm"
    ("Normalize and validate the parent and each contracted reusable child definition."
     "Index nets by driver and sink endpoint; validate all pin directions, types, modes, and complete routing."
     "For each external FOUR valuation, initialize every internal net to neither and assign external input driver nets."
     "Evaluate each child black-box table from its current input nets; join each produced output into its unique driver net."
     "Repeat until no bit changes. The lattice has two independently grow-only bits per net, so convergence is finite; an implementation bound detects defects."
     "Read external output sink nets, canonicalize the complete behavior table, and compare it byte-semantically to the declared table."
     "Traverse the verified containment family from the root, derive every contextual address, and compare it exactly with the normalized sovereign assembly placements."
     "At a contracted boundary, decode the provider's exact public leaf from its signed Agent Card, use it unchanged as the consumer-board die, and refuse role-derived replacement behavior."))
  ("error-paths"
    ((map ("class" "shape") ("codes" ("malformed-circuit" "circuit-limit" "incomplete-behavior")))
     (map ("class" "semantic") ("codes" ("nonmonotone-behavior" "pin-type-mismatch" "mode-mismatch" "behavior-mismatch")))
     (map ("class" "sovereignty") ("codes" ("assembly-root-mismatch" "unplaced-circuit" "unknown-placement" "component-drift" "missing-component")))
     (map ("class" "consensus") ("codes" ("consensus-leak" "unsettled-par")))
     (map ("class" "routing") ("codes" ("unknown-pin" "unrouted-pin" "nonconvergent-circuit")))))
  ("resource-use" "The first bounded profile allows at most six external FOUR inputs, hence 4096 behavior rows. Structural validation is linear in ports, instances, nets, and endpoints except the explicit monotonicity audit, which is quadratic in behavior rows. Later symbolic proof profiles may replace exhaustive tables only through a versioned profile and preserved equivalence vectors.")
  ("evidence" "test/hierarchical-circuit.test.mjs must prove deterministic identity, recursive composition, scale-field rejection, embedded-membrane rejection, reusable-definition placement under distinct sovereign occurrences, missing-placement refusal, signed black-box leaf decoding, public-interior refusal, tensor consensus rejection, and declared-versus-synthesized behavior mismatch refusal."))
